<title>UK: Potential cost VAT cases 200 mln stg -Treasury.</title>
<headline>Potential cost VAT cases 200 mln stg -Treasury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The potential cost of value added tax cases against the UK tax collection authorities would be around 200 million stg, the UK Treasury said.  </p>
<p>The European Court upheld on Thursday a move by Unilever subsidiary Elida Faberge and retail chain Argos to have the British government pay back excess VAT paid on discounted goods.</p>
<p>The court said in such cases VAT was payable on the discounted and not the full price, a decision that could require substantial repayments to companies from the British government.  </p>
<p>The Treasury said some press reports that the ruling could cost billions of lost revenue were mistaken and the potential cost of Argos style voucher schemes alone would be just 65 million stg.</p>
<p>-- John Speck, London Newsroom +44 171 542-8663</p>
